    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0342" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg270"/>

                <head>Argyle Square Junior Members Society</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Argyle Square Junior Members’ Society</hi>, <lb/> 24
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Grafton Place, Euston Square,
                            <placeName>London</placeName></hi>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1865-05-06">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 6, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to hand you a copy of a resolution
                    passed at a general meeting of this society, held last evening, expressing
                    condolence with the American nation on the late disastrous assassination of Mr.
                    Lincoln.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be your excellency’s most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. FRANCIS MORSE, </signed>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Hon. Sec</hi>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps"> C. F. Adams</hi>.</p>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Resolved</hi>, That this meeting desires to give
                        utterence to the feelings of grief With which it has heard of the
                        assassination of President Lincoln, and to convey to Mrs. Lincoln, and to
                        the United States government and people, an expresssion of their deepest
                        sympathy and condolence.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
